BigDecimal C++ contains a native C++ adaptation of mathematical algorithms and
observable behavior from OpenJDK 23.0.2, including work covered by notices for
Oracle and/or its affiliates and IBM Corporation. The adapted source is
distributed under GNU General Public License version 2 with the Classpath
exception reproduced in LICENSE.

The C++ representation, API adaptations, tests, examples, and native build
integration include changes made for this project. The C++ library does not
require a Java runtime to build or run. Its serialization codec intentionally
uses the documented Java Object Serialization wire format for interoperability.
